WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:01.429
OK.

00:00:01.429 --> 00:00:07.749
I want to have a conversation about polling
that is a careful conversation and a sober

00:00:07.749 --> 00:00:13.820
conversation, because there's been a narrative
building over the last maybe 10 to 14 days

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.580
that Biden is falling.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.990
And Trump is rising.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:23.750
And that this is objectively a disaster for
Joe Biden and Donald Trump has actually applied

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.950
the term plunging for George.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:30.320
Now, not not for someone's neck line, who
he's trying to talk to, but plunging from

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.099
the standpoint of Joe Biden's polling.

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:38.079
Now, the reality is, when we started getting
these polls two months ago that said Biden

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:41.560
is up by 10, Biden is up by 12.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.560
Biden is up by 15.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:48.160
I told you, Joe Biden is not going to win
the popular vote by 15, nor by 12, nor by

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.160
10.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.590
The polls are going to tighten.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:53.790
And depending on how you look at it, the polls
are tightening.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:01:00.510
Joe Biden is starting to campaign in a bit
of a different way as a result as we get closer

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:01.510
to the election.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:02.510
And that makes sense.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:07.500
Donald Trump tweeting, as I told you yesterday,
quote, Joe Biden is coming out of the basement

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.640
earlier than his hoped for ten days because
his people told him he has no choice.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.800
His poll numbers are plunging.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.920
So let's know the facts.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.800
But let's also not become overconfident as
a result of those facts.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.960
So, first of all, have the polling average
has tightened?

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:31.360
You can always find one poll that will say
almost whatever you want.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.930
But what about the averages?

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:38.530
The real Clear Politics average was Biden
plus nine point five.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.330
A couple of months ago.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.800
And it's tightened by a couple of points to
Biden plus seven, OK?

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.250
It's tighter.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:50.200
We never really expected Biden to win by 10
in the popular vote would have been completely

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.200
historic.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.990
And indeed, the numbers have tightened from
Biden with a nearly 10 point lead to a seven

00:01:54.990 --> 00:02:00.740
point lead in the 538 polling average model.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.960
You see that Joe Biden now is plus seven point
seven.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.229
At one point he was plus nine point six.

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:07.920
That was back in early July.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.509
So, yes, the polls have tightened.

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:12.040
Is Joe Biden plunging?

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.069
No, the answer is no.

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:16.439
And of course, Donald Trump lies all the time.

00:02:16.439 --> 00:02:19.889
He lies and says coronaviruses surging in
New Zealand when it's not.

00:02:19.889 --> 00:02:22.640
He says he's done a great job on the virus
when he is not.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.030
He said in April, fifteen cases would soon
be zero.

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:26.030
That didn't happen.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.059
We have six million.

00:02:27.059 --> 00:02:34.519
Just because Donald Trump is wrong about Joe
Biden's polling plunging doesn't mean Trump

00:02:34.519 --> 00:02:36.980
can't necessarily win.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.230
And that's where I want to sort of go next.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:46.669
It's really important that our actions not
be influenced by these dumb narratives that

00:02:46.669 --> 00:02:50.040
are put out there, either by Donald Trump
or others is poll.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.819
If polling is tightening, you have to vote
and I have to vote.

00:02:52.819 --> 00:02:55.849
If polling is not tightening, you have to
vote and I have to vote.

00:02:55.849 --> 00:02:59.799
If Trump is true, is right that Biden's polling
is plunging, you have to vote and I have to

00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:00.900
vote.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.120
That's the primary message here.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.730
And I know it's like a broken record at this
point, but you're only going to have to deal

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:09.730
with it for two, two more months, which are
arguably going to be long months, but it's

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:10.889
only two more months.

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:13.069
And as a reminder.

00:03:13.069 --> 00:03:18.129
If you go back to September 1st of 2016 and
look at the polling between Hillary Clinton

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:24.469
and Donald Trump, September one, 2016 for
Mike, four years ago today, Hillary Clinton

00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:26.269
was plus four point nine.

00:03:26.269 --> 00:03:30.809
And, of course, we know she ultimately lost
the electoral college.

00:03:30.809 --> 00:03:32.900
Is Biden's lead bigger as of today?

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.629
Yes, it's almost three points bigger than
Hillary's.

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:37.060
Four years ago.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.060
But so what?

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:39.319
Why take a chance?

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:42.540
Because there are things going on this year
that are not in the polls.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:48.560
In other words, voter purges are not part
of Biden's seven point lead right now.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.609
Planned voter suppression is not part of the
seven point lead Joe Biden has right now,

00:03:54.609 --> 00:03:58.659
messing with vote by mail and the post office
and everything we've been talking about for

00:03:58.659 --> 00:04:00.089
the last six weeks.

00:04:00.089 --> 00:04:02.769
That is not in the polls right now.

00:04:02.769 --> 00:04:04.749
Voter intimidation at the polls.

00:04:04.749 --> 00:04:08.760
This vague idea that there might be someone
who knows a militia, troops who who knows

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.650
what at the polls intimidating voters.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.189
That's not in the polls.

00:04:13.189 --> 00:04:15.930
So let's act as if.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:22.550
Remember, your vote could decide the outcome
of your state individually.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:26.740
It's unlikely any of our one votes will do
that.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:31.610
But collectively, if we all thought our vote
didn't matter and stayed home, we actually

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:33.919
would be influencing the results of the states.

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:36.050
So that's the correct approach.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:37.430
There's no downside.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.710
Joe Biden's polling is not plunging.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.379
It's tightening as expected.

00:04:41.379 --> 00:04:42.810
We've got about eight weeks to go.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:44.520
And this is the time up.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.930
Let me know where you are on the polling.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.629
I'm on Twitter at the Spackman.

00:04:48.629 --> 00:04:56.050
And remember that you can get the daily audio
podcast every single day on whichever is your

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:58.319
preferred podcasting platform.

00:04:58.319 --> 00:05:06.400
I tunes stitcher, Google Play, Spotify, Pandora
Pod, Biehn, etc..

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.400
There's a lot of them.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:34.539
We'll see you in just a couple

00:05:34.539 --> 00:06:22.760
of minutes.

